==English==
===Etymology===
Originally The Bailey, a street running outside the western wall of medieval London; from the word "bailey," a Middle English term for the outermost wall or court of a fortification.  The name became attached to the court established nearby in the 16th century, alongside Newgate Prison; officially known today as London's Central Criminal Court.

